<Layout title='Website privacy' description='How nrth.group handles an inquiry, browser preferences, private editorial sessions and optional website measurement.'>
 <header class='page-heading'><span class='section-label'>Website information · October 10, 2026</span><h1>Your privacy.</h1><p>A description of the public NRTH website. Products and services may require separate information for their own operation.</p></header>
 <article class='legal-prose'><h2>An introduction you control.</h2><p>Writing and reviewing an inquiry happens in your browser. The message is submitted to this website only when you choose Send inquiry. The submitted details include your name, email, optional organization, selected conversation and message.</p><p>If delivery is configured, the website uses Resend to submit the message to the relevant NRTH inbox. Acceptance by that service does not mean a person has read it. If delivery cannot be confirmed, the page preserves your message and provides alternatives: copy it, save it or open it in your email application. Sending through that application is a separate action under your control.</p><p>The information you share is used to respond to your introduction. Correspondence may remain in an NRTH mailbox. Contact NRTH to ask about access to or deletion of the information in your inquiry.</p><h2>Interaction and preferences.</h2><p>The site's visual experiments run in your browser. Saving an arrangement creates an image download; it does not create an account, commercial order or service request. The motion preference is stored locally. The site also respects the device setting for reduced motion.</p><h2>Hosting and measurement.</h2><p>Vercel processes technical requests to host the website. Fonts and default artwork are served with the site. Published content can include approved images delivered from Sanity's image service when the content system is connected.</p><p>When enabled for a deployment, Vercel Web Analytics records page visits and limited interactions such as venture discovery. Names, inquiry text, email addresses and organizations are not included in those events. Query parameters are removed from page measurement URLs. This site does not include advertising trackers.</p><h2>Private editorial access.</h2><p>An editor who signs in to the draft workspace receives a private, time-limited session cookie. Public visitors do not need an account to browse the portfolio.</p><h2>Keep sensitive details out.</h2><p>Do not include medical records, account passwords, payment details or other sensitive information in a general website inquiry. Product-specific data handling should be established through the appropriate separate process.</p><h2>Ask about this website.</h2><p>Use <a href='/contact'>Contact NRTH</a> to ask about privacy or the information in an introduction you have shared.</p></article>
</Layout>
